; ============================================================
; TITLE:    Word Spiral
; CATEGORY: Words & Text
; LEVEL:    Beginner
; TAGS:     label, spiral, letters, color, foreach
; SUMMARY:  Writes a sentence letter by letter along a growing spiral, with each letter a little bigger and a different color.
; ============================================================
;
; WHAT IT DOES
;   The turtle walks a spiral from the middle of the screen outwards.
;   After every step it writes the next letter of a sentence, so the
;   words curl around like the shell of a snail. Letters get bigger as
;   the spiral grows, and the colors cycle through the palette.
;
; HOW TO USE
;   Press Run. Change the sentence on the last line to spiral your own
;   words, for example   spiral [happy birthday to you]
;
; CONCEPTS YOU WILL LEARN
;   * walking through the letters of a word with FOREACH
;   * a spiral: turn the same amount each time, but walk further
;   * LABEL writes at the turtle's position, PENUP keeps the path hidden
;   * counter variables that grow a little on every pass
;
; THINGS TO TRY
;   * Turn 20 degrees instead of 25 for a looser spiral
;   * Put the pen down to see the path the turtle follows
;   * Make the letters shrink instead, starting from the outside
; ============================================================

; Glue the words of the sentence together with a dot between them, so
; you can still see where each word ends.
to joinup :sent
  if emptyp butfirst :sent [output first :sent]
  output (word first :sent ". joinup butfirst :sent)
end

to spiral :sent
  clearscreen hideturtle setbackground 0
  penup
  localmake "text joinup :sent
  localmake "stepsize 8
  localmake "n 0
  foreach :text [
    make "n :n + 1
    setpencolor 1 + remainder :n 14
    ; letters are a little taller than the step, so they nearly touch
    localmake "size :stepsize + 3
    setlabelheight :size
    ; LABEL draws from the bottom left corner of the letter, so shift
    ; back a little to center it on the spiral path, then come back.
    localmake "here pos
    setxy (xcor - :size / 3) (ycor - :size / 3)
    label ?
    setpos :here
    forward :stepsize
    right 25
    ; both the steps and the letters grow as we spiral outwards
    make "stepsize :stepsize + 0.3
    wait 2
  ]
end

spiral [once upon a time a little turtle walked around and around in circles ~
  writing every letter of this sentence as it went until it reached the edge]
